[{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Find all the missing angles and sides in the following right-angled triangles, giving your answers to three significant figures.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q1a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q1b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=40^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin50^\\circ=\\frac{19}{AC}\\Rightarrow AC=\\frac{19}{\\sin50^\\circ}=24.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>sf.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC=\\sqrt{24.802\\ldots^2-19^2}=15.9\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>sf.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC=\\sqrt{30^2-26^2}=15.0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>sf.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos B=\\frac{26}{30}\\Rightarrow B=\\arccos\\frac{13}{15}=29.9^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>sf.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C=60.1^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>sf.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>The diagram below shows the kite <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABCD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"DAC=60^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ACD=30^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It is also given that the length of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AD\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m. Find the exact area of the kite.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\" data-display=\"false\"></span> be the intersection of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"DB\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABCD\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a kite, the diagonals <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"DB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> meet at right-angles.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\cos60^\\circ =\\frac{XA}1\\Rightarrow XA=\\cos60^\\circ=\\frac12\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sin60^\\circ =\\frac{XD}1\\Rightarrow XD=\\sin60^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\tan30^\\circ =\\frac{XD}{XC}\\Rightarrow\\tan30^\\circ=\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt3}2}{XC}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow XC =\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt3}2}{\\tan30^\\circ}=\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt3}2}{\\frac{\\sqrt3}3}=\\frac32\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\text{Area} =2\\times\\frac12\\times XD\\times XA+2\\times\\frac12\\times XD\\times XC\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =XD\\times XA+XD\\times XC=\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\times\\frac12+\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\times\\frac32=\\sqrt3\\text{ m}^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>In the diagram below, the angles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"CDE\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are both <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"90^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and the length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"DE\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m. It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BCD\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a straight line. The area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is one third of the area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"CFE\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the exact length of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q3.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta =\\frac{CD}{DE}\\Rightarrow\\tan\\theta=\\frac{CD}1\\Rightarrow CD=\\tan\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\text{Area of triangle }CDE =\\frac12\\times1\\times\\tan\\theta=\\frac12\\tan\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\text{Area of triangle }ABC =\\frac13\\times\\frac12\\tan\\theta=\\frac16\\tan\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\tan\\theta =\\frac{BC}{AB}\\Rightarrow BC=AB\\tan\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times AB\\times BC =\\frac16\\tan\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac12\\times AB\\times(AB\\tan\\theta) =\\frac16\\tan\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac12AB^2 =\\frac16\\Rightarrow AB^2=\\frac13\\Rightarrow AB=\\frac{\\sqrt3}3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>In the diagram below, the angles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"OAB\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"OBC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"OCD\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are all <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"90^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and the lengths <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"CD\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are all <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> unit.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q4.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find the length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"OA\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{OD}{OA}=\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"OB^2 =1^2+OA^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"OC^2 =1^2+OB^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"OD^2 =1^2+OC^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore OD^2 =1+(1+OB^2)=1+(1+(1+OA^2))\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow OD^2 =3+OA^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{OD}{OA} =\\frac{\\sqrt{3+OA^2}}{OA}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3+OA^2}}{\\sqrt{OA^2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{3+OA^2}{OA^2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac3{OA^2}+1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{\\frac3{OA^2}+1} =\\sqrt2\\Rightarrow\\frac3{OA^2}+1=2\\Rightarrow\\frac3{OA^2}=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow OA^2 =3\\Rightarrow OA=\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>Find the area of the triangle shown in the diagram below, giving your answer to three significant figures.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q5.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<p>Area <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=\\frac12\\times23\\times44\\times\\sin75^\\circ=489\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>sf.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a triangle where angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"45^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, side <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm, and side <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC=15\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm. Find the length of side <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a^2 =b^2+c^2-2bc\\cos A\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"AC^2 =AB^2+BC^2-2\\times AB\\times BC\\times\\cos(\\angle ABC)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow AC^2 =20^2+15^2-2\\times20\\times15\\times\\cos45^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow AC^2 =625-300\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow AC =\\sqrt{625-300\\sqrt2}=14.2\\text{ cm to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a triangle where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm, and angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ACB=40^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Use the sine rule to find two possible values for angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BAC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answers to one decimal place.</p></li><li><p>Hence draw and label two possible triangles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sin40^\\circ}9 =\\frac{\\sin A}{12}\\Rightarrow\\sin A=\\frac{12\\sin40^\\circ}9=0.857\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow A =\\arcsin0.857\\ldots=59.0^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\text{Or }A =180-\\arcsin0.857\\ldots=121.0^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/solutions/assets/diagrams/s7b1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/solutions/assets/diagrams/s7b2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Find all the missing angles and sides in the following triangles, giving your answers to three significant figures.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q8a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q8b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q8c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sin A}8 =\\frac{\\sin75^\\circ}{11}\\Rightarrow\\sin A=\\frac{8\\sin75^\\circ}{11}=0.702\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow A =\\arcsin0.702\\ldots=44.6\\text{ to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow C =180^\\circ-75^\\circ-44.6\\ldots=60.4^\\circ\\text{ to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{AB}{\\sin C} =\\frac{BC}{\\sin A}\\Rightarrow\\frac{AB}{\\sin60.372\\ldots}=\\frac8{\\sin44.627\\ldots}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow AB =\\frac{\\sin60.372\\ldots}{\\sin44.627\\ldots}=9.90\\text{ to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"12^2 =11^2+9^2-2\\times11\\times9\\times\\cos A\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\cos A =\\frac{11^2+9^2-12^2}{2\\times11\\times9}=\\frac{29}{99}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow A =\\arccos\\frac{29}{99}=73.0^\\circ\\text{ to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sin B}{11} =\\frac{\\sin72.9\\ldots^\\circ}{12}\\Rightarrow\\sin B=0.876\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow B =\\arcsin0.876\\ldots=61.2^\\circ\\text{ to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C =180^\\circ-72.9\\ldots^\\circ-61.2\\ldots^\\circ=45.8^\\circ\\text{ to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Triangle 1 (this is not how it is drawn in the question, but satisfies the given information):</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sin B}{14} =\\frac{\\sin33^\\circ}9\\Rightarrow\\sin B=\\frac{14\\sin33^\\circ}9=0.847\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow B =\\arcsin0.847\\ldots=57.9^\\circ\\text{ to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow A =180^\\circ-33^\\circ-57.9\\ldots=89.1^\\circ\\text{ to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"BC^2 =9^2+14^2-2\\times9\\times14\\times\\cos89.0\\ldots^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow BC^2 =272.997\\ldots\\Rightarrow BC=16.5\\text{ m to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Or</p>","<p>Triangle 2 (this is how it appears to be drawn in the question, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> obtuse and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> acute):</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sin B}{14} =\\frac{\\sin33^\\circ}9\\Rightarrow\\sin B=\\frac{14\\sin33^\\circ}9=0.847\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow B =180^\\circ-\\arcsin0.847\\ldots=122^\\circ\\text{ to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow A =180^\\circ-33^\\circ-122.0\\ldots=24.9^\\circ\\text{ to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"BC^2 =9^2+14^2-2\\times9\\times14\\times\\cos24.9\\ldots^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow BC^2 =48.443\\ldots\\Rightarrow BC=6.96\\text{ m to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>Find the area of the triangle shown in the diagram below, giving your answer to three significant figures.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q9.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\angle ACB=180^\\circ-68^\\circ-58^\\circ=54^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{AC}{\\sin68^\\circ}=\\frac{3.8}{\\sin54^\\circ}\\Rightarrow AC=4.355\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm.</p>","<p>Area <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times3.8\\times4.355\\ldots\\times\\sin58^\\circ=7.02\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>sf.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a triangle where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm and angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BAC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The area of the triangle is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the two possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to one decimal place.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25=\\frac12\\times16\\times9\\times\\sin x\\Rightarrow\\sin x=\\frac{25}{72}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow x=\\arcsin\\frac{25}{72}=20.317\\ldots^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=20.3^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"180^\\circ-20.317\\ldots^\\circ=159.7^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>dp.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>The diagram below shows the triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It is given that angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ACB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is obtuse. Find the length of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BX\" data-display=\"false\"></span> bisects the triangle.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q11.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sin30^\\circ}6=\\frac{\\sin C}{10}\\Rightarrow\\sin C=\\frac56\\Rightarrow C=\\arcsin\\frac56=56.442\\ldots^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>However, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is obtuse, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C=180^\\circ-56.442\\ldots^\\circ=123.557\\ldots^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\angle ABC=180^\\circ-30^\\circ-123.557\\ldots^\\circ=26.442\\ldots^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC=\\frac12\\times10\\times6\\times\\sin26.442\\ldots^\\circ=13.359\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XBC=\\frac12\\times13.359\\ldots=6.679\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\frac12\\times6\\times XC=6.679\\ldots\\Rightarrow XC=2.67\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>sf.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a triangle where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2m^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm and angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BAC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"45^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The area of the triangle is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"640\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=k\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is an integer to be found.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"640 =\\frac12\\times5m\\times2m^2\\times\\sin45^\\circ\\Rightarrow640=5m^3\\times\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow m^3 =128\\sqrt2\\Rightarrow m^3=\\sqrt{32768}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow m =\\left((32768)^{\\frac12}\\right)^{\\frac13}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow m =\\left((32768)^{\\frac13}\\right)^{\\frac12}=32^{\\frac12}=4\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore k =4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>The diagram below shows the triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"11x-4x^2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the largest angle in the triangle.</p></li></ol><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q13.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3x+1)^2 =(2x+1)^2+(3\\sqrt3x)^2-2(2x+1)(3\\sqrt3x)\\cos30^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow(3x+1)^2 =(2x+1)^2+27x^2-2(2x+1)(3\\sqrt3x)\\times\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow9x^2+6x+1 =4x^2+4x+1+27x^2-(2x+1)\\times9x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow9x^2+6x+1 =4x^2+4x+1+27x^2-18x^2-9x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow9x^2+6x+1 =13x^2-5x+1\\Rightarrow11x-4x^2=0\\text{ as required}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"11x-4x^2=0\\Rightarrow(11-4x)x=0\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{11}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\neq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The largest angle is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BAC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3\\sqrt3\\times\\tfrac{11}4)^2 =(3\\times\\tfrac{11}4+1)^2+(2\\times\\tfrac{11}4+1)^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" \\quad-2\\times(3\\times\\tfrac{11}4+1)\\times(2\\times\\tfrac{11}4+1)\\times\\cos A\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac{3267}{16} =\\frac{1369}{16}+\\frac{169}4-\\frac{481}4\\cos A\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\cos A =\\frac{\\frac{1369}{16}+\\frac{169}4-\\frac{3267}{16}}{\\frac{481}4}=-\\frac{47}{74}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow A =\\arccos(-\\tfrac{47}{74})=129^\\circ\\text{ to }3\\text{sf}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>The diagram below shows a parallelogram with sides of length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"86\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"140\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm. It is given that angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC=120^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that the exact area of the parallelogram is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a rational number.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q14.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\text{Area} =2\\times\\frac12\\times0.86\\times1.4\\times\\sin120^\\circ=1.204\\times\\frac{\\sqrt3}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =0.602\\times\\sqrt3=\\frac{301}{500}\\sqrt3\\text{ m}^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>It is given that a triangle has sides of length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The largest angle in the triangle is labelled <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Use the cosine rule to show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos x=\\frac{b-3}{2b}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the largest angle, it must be opposite the largest side, which is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\therefore(b+2)^2 =(b+1)^2+b^2-2(b+1)b\\cos x\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\cos x =\\frac{(b+1)^2+b^2-(b+2)^2}{2(b+1)b}=\\frac{b^2+2b+1+b^2-(b^2+4b+4)}{2(b+1)b}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =\\frac{b^2-2b-3}{2(b+1)b}=\\frac{(b+1)(b-3)}{2(b+1)b}=\\frac{b-3}{2b}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>Ben measures the angle of elevation from where he is standing to the top of a tall building to be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30.5^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. He then walks straight towards the building for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres, stops, and measures the angle of elevation again. This time it is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"42.7^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Determine the height of the building.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q16.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\angle ABC=180^\\circ-42.7^\\circ=137.3^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\angle BCA=180^\\circ-137.3^\\circ-30.5^\\circ=12.2^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{BC}{\\sin30.5^\\circ}=\\frac{20}{\\sin12.2^\\circ}\\Rightarrow BC=\\frac{20\\sin30.5^\\circ}{\\sin12.2^\\circ}=48.033\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin42.7^\\circ=\\frac{OC}{48.033\\ldots}\\Rightarrow OC=32.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>sf.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>Three archaeological digs, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, are drawn on a map. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"180\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres due South of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"320\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on a bearing of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"075^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the bearing of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the bearing of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the bearing of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/solutions/assets/diagrams/s17.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Bearing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"180^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ-105^\\circ=255^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Bearing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"255^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\angle BAC =180^\\circ-75=105^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"BC^2 =AB^2+AC^2-2\\times AB\\times AC\\times\\cos105^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =180^2+320^2-2\\times180\\times320\\times\\cos105^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" =164615.95\\ldots\\Rightarrow BC=405.7289\\ldots\\text{ m}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\sin(ACB)}{180} =\\frac{\\sin105^\\circ}{405.7289\\ldots}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\angle ACB =\\arcsin\\left(\\frac{180\\sin105^\\circ}{405.7289\\ldots}\\right)=25.374\\ldots^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"360^\\circ-105^\\circ-25.374\\ldots^\\circ =229.625\\ldots^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Bearing <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"230^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>The diagram below shows a triangle, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, with sides of length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\angle ABC=60^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q18.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"10^2 =p^2+(p+5)^2-2\\times p\\times(p+5)\\times\\cos60^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow100 =p^2+(p+5)^2-p(p+5)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow100 =p^2+p^2+10p+25-p^2-5p\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow0 =p^2+5p-75\\Rightarrow p=\\frac{-5\\pm5\\sqrt{13}}2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=\\frac{-5+5\\sqrt{13}}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q19","number":19,"question":"<p>The area of a regular pentagon is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"60\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Calculate the length of one of its sides.</p>","steps":["<p>Divide the pentagon into five triangles, so each triangle will have an area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{60}5=12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{360}5=72^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>We will call the distance from the centre of the pentagon to a vertex <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times r^2\\times\\sin72^\\circ=12\\Rightarrow r=5.023\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l^2=5.023\\ldots^2+5.023\\ldots^2-2\\times5.023\\ldots\\times5.023\\ldots\\times\\cos72^\\circ\\Rightarrow l=5.91\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>sf.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q20","number":20,"question":"<p>The area of a regular octagon is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"450\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Calculate the length of one of its sides.</p>","steps":["<p>Divide the octagon into eight triangles, so each triangle will have an area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{450}8=56.25\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{360}8=45^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>We will call the distance from the centre of the octagon to a vertex <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times r^2\\times\\sin45^\\circ=56.25\\Rightarrow r=12.61\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l^2=12.61\\ldots^2+12.61\\ldots^2-2\\times12.61\\ldots\\times12.61\\ldots\\times\\cos45^\\circ\\Rightarrow l=9.65\" data-display=\"false\"></span> cm to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>sf.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.39-q21","number":21,"question":"<p>The diagram below shows a square, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABCD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, with area <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"100\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> drawn on the coordinate axes. The square has been divided up into four triangles, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XBC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XAB\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XCD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XAD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, with areas <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"40\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> respectively.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/questions/assets/diagrams/q21.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has exact coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(p,q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has exact coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(r,q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;r&lt;p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XYD\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has an area that is at least half of the area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XAD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the range of possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XBC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has area <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so shortest distance from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times2\\times10=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Likewise, triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XAB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has area <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so shortest distance from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"X\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times4\\times10=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore X\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(8,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XAD\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"40\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>So area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XYD\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is at least <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"XD=\\sqrt{8^2+6^2}=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"YX\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"DC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are parallel, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\angle YXD=\\angle XDC=\\arctan\\frac68=\\arctan\\frac34=36.869\\ldots^\\circ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore\\frac12\\times XY\\times10\\times\\sin(\\arctan\\frac34)\\geq20\\Rightarrow XY\\geq\\frac{20}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore0&lt;r\\leq(8-\\frac{20}3)=\\frac43\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow0&lt;r\\leq\\frac43\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.39/solutions/assets/diagrams/s21b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]}]